      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing OCR Provider**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Vision API for the OCR task in `extract_text.py`. It provides strong OCR capabilities, which should fit the user's needs well. I will include the necessary Google Cloud Vision API key and identify the choice in the Python code.\n\n\n**Implementing OCR Extraction**\n\nI'm now fully committed to implementing the `extract_text.py` file, utilizing the Google Cloud Vision API. My plan includes importing the `google.cloud.vision_v1p5beta1` library and creating a function designed to extract text from images. This function will accept either an image path or the image content itself as input, using the `ImageAnnotatorClient` to execute text detection and then return the extracted text. I'm ready to begin coding now.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789866857659,
          "start": 1789866856147
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc60ced3001sntxyzVU4mAUb6",
